(136,"Retries on flaky tools (p=0.3 failure)?","Success rose 0.401 → 0.924 on Day 136."),
(136,"Memory pitfall seen on Day 136?","Top-1 memory retrieval returned stale facts after updates."),
(137,"Why sandbox a code tool?","Model-written code is untrusted; limit CPU, memory, time, filesystem and network."),
(137,"Day 137 sandbox lesson?","rlimits alone still leaked filesystem access; resource limits are not isolation."),
(138,"pass^k?","Success in all k trials: a reliability metric (noisy pass^8 was 0.458 on Day 138)."),
(138,"Why a failure taxonomy?","Counting failure types (bad args, wrong tool, loop, hallucinated result) tells you what to fix."),
(139,"Indirect prompt injection?","Instructions hidden in retrieved documents or tool outputs that the model then follows."),
(139,"Injection result on Day 139?","Undefended, it queued 22/24 emails; with an allow-list and approval gate, 0."),
(139,"Constrained decoding on Day 139?","24/24 outputs valid JSON, but only 18/24 correct: valid is not right."),
(140,"Project W20 lesson?","Defences that do not depend on detecting the attack (allow-lists, approval gates) are the reliable ones."),
(141,"First baseline in an ML product?","A simple rule; on Day 141 a rule scored 0.804 vs the MLP's 0.965."),
(141,"Why pick a threshold by cost?","Errors cost different amounts; the metric should be the business cost, not accuracy."),
(142,"Reproducibility check on Day 142?","Same seed gave identical weight hashes."),
(142,"Lucky-seed selection?","Picking the best of many seeds overstates performance; report the spread."),
(143,"Experiment tracking stores?","Parameters, metrics, artifacts and code/data versions for each run (MLflow on Day 143)."),
(144,"ONNX Runtime speed-up on Day 144?","4.2× per call, but only about 1.15× over HTTP, where overhead dominates."),
(144,"Training/serving skew causes?","Different preprocessing code, stale or leaked features, different library versions or dtypes."),
(145,"PSI?","Σ (a − e)·ln(a/e) over bins of reference e and current a: a drift score."),
(145,"Fixed PSI>0.2 vs Bonferroni-KS on Day 145?","PSI>0.2 raised 48/50 false alarms; Bonferroni-corrected KS 2/50."),
(145,"Label-error loop result?","Fixing flagged labels raised accuracy 0.909 → 0.958."),
(145,"Does drift always hurt accuracy?","No; on Day 145 a detected drift did not hurt accuracy. Alert ≠ harm."),
(146,"Peeking at an A/B test?","Stopping when p<0.05 inflates false positives (FPR 0.191 on Day 146)."),
(146,"Batch vs online inference cost?","Batch was about 1000× cheaper under assumed prices on Day 146."),
(147,"Project W21 service p95?","21.7 ms on localhost."),
(147,"What is a model card?","A document of intended use, data, metrics, limits and ethical notes, shipped with the model."),
(148,"Why content-hash prompts?","An eval result is then tied to exact prompt text, not a reusable name."),
(148,"Day 148 prompt results (of 24)?","v1 zero-shot 0, v2 3-shot 7, v3 4-shot 13, v4 (v3 reworded) 13."),
(148,"Why did v2→v3 fail the gate?","v3 lost 3 cases v2 passed (1024/16, 99/3, 45%7) despite 13 vs 7 overall; McNemar p=0.146."),
(148,"Why McNemar for prompts?","Both prompts answer the same cases; only discordant cases carry information."),
(148,"When is a generation cache safe?","Deterministic decoding and a key with prompt hash, input, model and settings (24 hits, identical results on Day 148)."),
(148,"Seen vs held-out cases?","Tune on seen; held-out shows whether gains generalise (v3: seen 9/18, held-out 4/6)."),
